o I should file that. I’m wondering about transforming the seed shape and identifying all zero placements. The demo transforms might cover all orientations, but the outputs show copies that are rotated. It seems we can write a function to extract color from non-background connected objects, which involves finding placements where values equal zero. I’ll ensure the file creation is allowed and works in Python.","t":1792729576.6742237,"summary":true},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"import os\np='/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HPL0-prime-agent-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u011/system/state/workspace/programs/task-16f88db9.py'\nos.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p),exist_ok=True)\ncode='''from collections import deque\n\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    colors = {v for row in grid for v in row}\n    marker = max(colors)\n    cells = {(r, c) for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == marker}\n    # The marker depicts the shape to stamp at every all-zero match.\n    r0 = min(r for r,c in cells); c0 = min(c for r,c in cells)\n    shape = {(r-r0,c-c0) for r,c in cells}\n    sh, sw = max(r for r,c in shape)+1, max(c for r,c in shape)+1\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    for r in range(h-sh+1):\n        for c in range(w-sw+1):\n            if all(grid[r+dr][c+dc] == 0 for dr,dc in shape):\n                for dr,dc in shape:\n                    out[r+dr][c+dc] = marker\n    return out\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(code)\nprint(p, os.path.getsize(p))","t":1792729576.6742237,"stored":["programs/task-16f88db9.py"],"output":"/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HPL0-prime-agent-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u011/system/state/workspace/programs/task-16f88db9.py 733\n"}],"action":{"type":"finish"}}]}